From: Orkhan Javadli <ojavadli@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:07:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/18] tei-v7 struct-07: Add an explicit
 issue-to-acceptance-criteria decomposition g

---
 dars-agent/config/default_dars.yaml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dars-agent/config/default_dars.yaml b/dars-agent/config/default_dars.yaml
index a7f3ae3..5b7e587 100644
--- a/dars-agent/config/default_dars.yaml
+++ b/dars-agent/config/default_dars.yaml
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ system_template: |-
   </command_docs>
 
   General Guidelines:
-  1. First decompose the issue into behavior, affected code paths, and acceptance criteria before editing.
+  1. Before editing, write a compact issue model containing: requested behavior, current behavior, affected code paths, invariants, likely edge cases, and concrete acceptance criteria. Do not edit until these items are identified from the issue and repository evidence.
   2. Trace the relevant implementation and existing tests, then state a concrete patch hypothesis.
   3. Make the smallest coherent patch and inspect the resulting diff immediately.
   4. Run focused tests for the changed behavior before broader tests.
